{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphismConjecture","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.MassEndomorphismConjecture","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.fullMass_pos_of_vol_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.fullMass_pos_of_vol_pos","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-conjecture.lean#L161-L172","doc":"**Mass is positive when vol_identity > 0 and tr_descended ≥ 0.**\n\nUnder the natural physical conditions (positive volume, non-negative\ndescended trace), the full categorical mass is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.descended_eq_vol_minus_transient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.descended_eq_vol_minus_transient","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-conjecture.lean#L152-L159","doc":"**The descended part equals vol_identity minus the transient.**\n\nEquivalent rearrangement of `vol_eq` expressed for the descended piece. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.mass_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.mass_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-conjecture.lean#L143-L150","doc":"**fullMass = tr_descended + tr_transient** (explicit decomposition lemma).\n\nThis is definitional but stated as a lemma to make the two-term\nstructure available for downstream rewrites. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.fullMass_eq_descended_of_zero_transient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.fullMass_eq_descended_of_zero_transient","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-conjecture.lean#L131-L141","doc":"**In the flat case (tr_transient = 0), fullMass equals the descended part.**\n\nWhen the brane tower contributes nothing (all z_i = 0 or no\nblow-up centres), the full mass is entirely descended. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.transient_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.transient_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-conjecture.lean#L117-L129","doc":"**Transient is non-negative when vol_identity ≥ tr_descended.**\n\nIf the volume identity term dominates the descended trace, the\nbrane-tower contribution `tr_transient` is non-negative.  This is\nthe algebraic content of the physical expectation that the tower\nalways contributes positively to mass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.transient_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.transient_unique","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-conjecture.lean#L104-L115","doc":"**Transient part is uniquely determined by the class data.**\n\nGiven `vol_eq : tr_transient = vol_identity - tr_descended`,\nthere is exactly one value of tr_transient consistent with the\nclass — namely `vol_identity - tr_descended`.  Any other element\nsatisfying the same equation equals tr_transient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.braneTowerPartialSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.braneTowerPartialSum","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-conjecture.lean#L90-L98","doc":"The brane-tower partial sum at level N, conditional on a\n`MassEndomorphism` instance. Mirrors the\n`conj:brane-tower-z-habiro` Cauchy-sequence claim: the partial\nsums tr_transient stabilise as N grows, with the limit in the\nz-Habiro completion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.fullMass_eq_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.fullMass_eq_volume","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-conjecture.lean#L78-L88","doc":"Conditional theorem: under the mass-endomorphism conjecture, the\nfull categorical mass equals the volume identity term. This is\nproved unconditionally from the class instance — the only\n\"axiomatic\" input is the existence of the instance itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.fullMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.fullMass","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-conjecture.lean#L69-L76","doc":"The full categorical mass at brane-tower-saturation. Conditional\non a `MassEndomorphism` instance, this gives the mass as the sum\nof the descended Markov trace plus the transient brane-tower —\nfully derived from the class data, no further sorries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.MassEndomorphism.vol_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.MassEndomorphism.vol_eq","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-conjecture.lean#L67-L67","doc":"The volume identity as an equality. The proof of this equality\nis the open part of the conjecture; instances supply it as a\nhypothesis (axiomatic input). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.MassEndomorphism.vol_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.MassEndomorphism.vol_identity","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-conjecture.lean#L62-L62","doc":"The asserted volume identity:\ntr_transient = Vol(K_β)/ℏ_q² − |tr_descended|. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.MassEndomorphism.tr_descended","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.MassEndomorphism.tr_descended","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-conjecture.lean#L59-L59","doc":"The descended Markov-trace component: tr_M(ρ(β)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.MassEndomorphism.tr_transient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.MassEndomorphism.tr_transient","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-conjecture.lean#L57-L57","doc":"The transient (brane-tower) Markov-trace component:\ntr_M(Φ^trans(β)) = Σ_{i=1}^{N} Φ_q(z_i). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.MassEndomorphism.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.MassEndomorphism.z","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-conjecture.lean#L54-L54","doc":"The algebraic-volume coordinates z_i for i = 1..N. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.MassEndomorphism.N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.MassEndomorphism.N","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-conjecture.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The number of brane levels N (depends on the braid word β). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.MassEndomorphism.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.MassEndomorphism.q","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-conjecture.lean#L50-L50","doc":"The substrate parameter q ∈ R. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.MassEndomorphism.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.MassEndomorphism.mk","kind":"ctor","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-conjecture.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.MassEndomorphism","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.MassEndomorphism","kind":"class","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-conjecture.lean#L33-L67","doc":"The mass-endomorphism conjecture, encoded as a class.\n\nA `MassEndomorphism R β` instance asserts the existence of a\nclosed-form NF decomposition for the Hecke mass element Φ_mass(β).\nSpecifically, it provides:\n  - a finite list of generators (the NF basis) with coefficients,\n  - the transient (brane-tower) component as a Σ Φ_q(z_i),\n  - the algebraic-volume coordinates z_i,\n  - the substrate parameter q ∈ R.\n\nThe `vol_identity` field is the asserted equality\nΣ_i Φ_q(z_i) = Vol(K)/ℏ_q² — the topological-decomposition\npart of the conjecture (Step 2 in conj:mass-endomorphism's\n\"What is known\"). ","signatureChunk":0}]}